# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Client build-time config (Vite). Values are INLINED INTO THE JS BUNDLE at
# build time, so after changing anything you must rebuild and re-sync:
#     npm run build && npx cap sync android
#
# How to use: copy this file to `.env.local` (already git-ignored) and fill in
# the real values. Never commit real TURN credentials.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Backend / Socket.IO origin
VITE_API_URL=https://chat-app-backend-1yfa.onrender.com

# ---- ICE servers ----------------------------------------------------------
# STUN: the public Google STUN servers already hard-coded in the app are free
#       and excellent - you do NOT need to host your own STUN.
# TURN: required whenever a peer is behind symmetric NAT / mobile carrier
#       CGNAT. Without a working TURN a call "signals" fine but carries no
#       audio/video (silent call, black video).
#
# Comma-separated list is supported. A good set is:
#   turn:3478 udp   -> fastest, works most of the time
#   turns:5349 tcp  -> TLS, survives restrictive/corporate firewalls
#   turn:443 tcp    -> last-resort fallback (looks like HTTPS)
VITE_TURN_URL=turn:turn.example.com:3478?transport=udp,turns:turn.example.com:5349?transport=tcp
VITE_TURN_USERNAME=myuser
VITE_TURN_CREDENTIAL=mystrongpassword